    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Two clubs"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "In a class, some pupils are in the music club and some in the sports club, and some are in both. Union, intersection and difference let us talk about each group exactly."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "union",
          "intersection",
          "A - B",
          "complement",
          "disjoint sets",
          "De Morgan",
          "n(A U B)"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The union A U B contains elements that are in A or in B or in both.\nThe intersection A n B contains elements common to both A and B.\nThe difference A - B contains elements of A that are not in B.\nThe complement A' is the set of elements of the universal set U that are not in A.\nDisjoint sets have no common element, so A n B is empty.\nDe Morgan's laws: (A U B)' = A' n B' and (A n B)' = A' U B'.\nFor finite sets, n(A U B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A n B)."
        }
      },
